WEBVTT

00:00.910 --> 00:04.060
<i>It's the semi-finals of the National Middle School Football Tournament.</i>

00:04.060 --> 00:04.680
Here!

00:04.680 --> 00:08.980
<i>Less than 10 minutes remain in the second semi-final match between Nankatsu and Furano!</i>

00:04.680 --> 00:07.180
Furano! Furano!

00:07.180 --> 00:10.430
Hooray, hooray, Nankatsu!

00:08.980 --> 00:12.240
<i>While the first team to reach the finals for the third time in row,</i>

00:12.240 --> 00:14.150
<i>Toho Academy, watch this game closely,</i>

00:14.150 --> 00:17.400
<i>the fierce fight between two teams continue.</i>

00:17.400 --> 00:18.650
All right! Let's do this!

00:18.650 --> 00:21.950
<i>After falling behind, Furano have since regrouped,</i>

00:21.950 --> 00:25.170
<i>and are slowly regaining control of the pace of the match!</i>

00:25.170 --> 00:26.410
Persevere, guys!

00:26.410 --> 00:27.650
We'll score a goal!

00:27.650 --> 00:29.160
We'll tie this game!

00:29.160 --> 00:32.540
<i>Both teams are pouring their hearts and souls into this game!</i>

00:33.000 --> 00:36.040
<i>And it's been a fair match throughout, with no fouls in the game.</i>

00:36.690 --> 00:42.880
<i>The lively match between Nankatsu and Furano is a first-rate game with great fighting spirit, truly worthy of the semi-finals.</i>

00:43.760 --> 00:46.400
Go, Furano!

00:49.470 --> 00:52.510
<i>God, I'm begging you.</i>

00:52.510 --> 00:54.270
<i>Let them win!</i>

00:56.530 --> 00:59.240
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:56.530 --> 00:59.240
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:00.160 --> 01:02.830
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:00.160 --> 01:02.830
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:03.740 --> 01:06.450
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:03.740 --> 01:06.450
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:13.340 --> 01:16.170
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

01:13.340 --> 01:16.170
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

01:16.170 --> 01:22.430
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

01:16.170 --> 01:22.430
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

01:22.430 --> 01:28.310
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta no ni</i>

01:22.430 --> 01:28.310
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

01:28.310 --> 01:34.900
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

01:28.310 --> 01:34.900
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

01:34.900 --> 01:38.900
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

01:34.900 --> 01:38.900
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

01:38.900 --> 01:43.410
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

01:38.900 --> 01:43.410
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

01:43.410 --> 01:49.000
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

01:43.410 --> 01:49.000
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

01:49.000 --> 01:50.540
<i>baka darou?</i>

01:49.000 --> 01:50.540
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

01:50.540 --> 01:51.750
<i>ai</i>

01:50.540 --> 01:51.750
<i>Love!</i>

01:51.750 --> 01:55.250
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

01:51.750 --> 01:55.250
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

01:55.250 --> 02:05.140
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

01:55.250 --> 02:05.140
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

02:05.140 --> 02:05.970
<i>ai</i>

02:05.140 --> 02:05.970
<i>Love!</i>

02:05.970 --> 02:09.770
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

02:05.970 --> 02:09.770
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

02:09.770 --> 02:13.770
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

02:09.770 --> 02:13.770
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

02:13.770 --> 02:20.030
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

02:13.770 --> 02:20.030
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

02:20.030 --> 02:22.860
<i>hanasanai</i>

02:20.030 --> 02:22.860
<i>for a single moment!</i>

02:24.740 --> 02:30.240
<b><b>EPISODE 45:
TEARS AT THE AIRPORT</b></b>

02:24.960 --> 02:28.160
<i>Furano continues their fierce attack on Nankatsu's goal!</i>

02:28.160 --> 02:31.160
<i>Aiming for a goal, what will Furano do?</i>

02:31.160 --> 02:33.080
<i>Wakamatsu runs forward.</i>

02:34.660 --> 02:36.410
<i>Will he just go for a shot?</i>

02:37.360 --> 02:39.750
<i>No, Nankatsu block him off!</i>

02:39.750 --> 02:42.090
<i>They don't let him break through to the goal.</i>

02:42.090 --> 02:44.310
Nice, everyone!

02:44.310 --> 02:47.300
<i>Nankatsu have been called "Tsubasa's one-man team" before,</i>

02:47.300 --> 02:50.470
<i>but that couldn't be further from the truth.</i>

02:50.470 --> 02:53.620
<i>Even though he can't go all out right now as he normally does,</i>

02:53.620 --> 02:58.810
<i>the team is making up for it, helping each other and demonstrating brilliant play.</i>

02:59.390 --> 03:05.320
<i>And as their captain, Tsubasa is swallowing his pain and doing his best under these circumstances.</i>

02:59.390 --> 03:02.670
Iwami, one-two! Then pass it to Nagano!

03:06.010 --> 03:07.350
<i>I can clearly say it.</i>

03:07.350 --> 03:10.570
<i>Nankatsu is the best team in Japan.</i>

03:10.570 --> 03:13.380
<i>Furano steals the ball once again!</i>

03:13.380 --> 03:14.280
Nice cut!

03:14.280 --> 03:17.790
<i>This is proof of their tenacity to score a goal and tie the game.</i>

03:17.790 --> 03:19.380
You can do it! Keep fighting!

03:19.380 --> 03:21.100
<i>Good luck, guys.</i>

03:21.100 --> 03:25.660
<i>We're a team from the northern lands; they often said things like, we're weak against heat,</i>

03:25.660 --> 03:28.260
<i>or that we had no place in the race for the title.</i>

03:28.260 --> 03:29.720
<i>But... have a look at this.</i>

03:29.720 --> 03:34.470
<i>We have fairly won our way through the tournament among this heat, day after day.</i>

03:34.470 --> 03:37.770
<i>Just take a look! They've chased the reigning champions, Nankatsu, this far!</i>

03:37.770 --> 03:39.270
All right! Go!

03:39.270 --> 03:40.890
We'll surely have a chance!

03:40.890 --> 03:42.650
Don't give up, keep attacking!

03:42.650 --> 03:45.530
<i>No player other than Matsuyama might stand out....</i>

03:45.530 --> 03:47.650
<i>Still, they can do it if they try.</i>

03:47.650 --> 03:50.720
<i>I want to make you win.</i>

03:50.720 --> 03:51.280
Take this!

03:51.650 --> 03:53.300
<i>Furano gets the ball to the goal!</i>

03:53.300 --> 03:53.990
Good!

03:54.990 --> 03:56.410
<i>Morisaki punches it away!</i>

03:56.410 --> 03:58.250
<i>Furano can't score again!</i>

03:58.250 --> 03:59.510
Okay, here we go!

03:59.510 --> 04:00.960
This time, we'll attack!

04:00.960 --> 04:01.710
Yeah!

04:01.710 --> 04:05.540
<i>Nankatsu finally get a chance
to mount an attack after a long while!</i>

04:05.540 --> 04:06.710
Get back, everyone!

04:06.710 --> 04:08.460
We have to get back immediately!

04:08.460 --> 04:10.510
<i>Nankatsu are on the offensive...</i>

04:10.510 --> 04:13.890
<i>If they score another one now, the game will be decided.</i>

04:13.890 --> 04:16.970
<i>Who will Izawa send a pass to?</i>

04:16.970 --> 04:18.600
Eat this!

04:18.600 --> 04:21.190
<i>Oh, it's an unexpected attack on the goal from Izawa!</i>

04:21.190 --> 04:22.480
Like I'd let that in!

04:23.190 --> 04:25.510
<i>The goalkeeper Kato reacts to it in time!</i>

04:25.510 --> 04:27.650
<i>But the ball falls right in front of Taki.</i>

04:29.650 --> 04:31.400
<i>This goal will seal the deal!</i>

04:33.620 --> 04:35.320
<i>Furano block this off too!</i>

04:35.320 --> 04:36.450
Guys!

04:36.450 --> 04:38.950
<i>Now the ball falls right in front of the goal!</i>

04:38.950 --> 04:40.660
I've got this!

04:40.660 --> 04:43.000
<i>A sliding shot from Kisugi!</i>

04:43.000 --> 04:44.340
<i>But no, it won't go in!</i>

04:44.340 --> 04:45.250
<i>Furano deflect it!</i>

04:45.250 --> 04:48.710
<i>Matsuyama stopped marking Tsubasa for this, excellent judgment!</i>

04:48.710 --> 04:49.420
Ah!

04:49.420 --> 04:52.670
<i>But the cleared ball finds its way right in front of Tsubasa!</i>

04:52.670 --> 04:53.430
Crap!

04:56.680 --> 04:57.800
Drive...

05:00.610 --> 05:01.890
Shot!

05:08.770 --> 05:11.230
<i>Matsuyama blocks it with his entire body!</i>

05:11.230 --> 05:13.150
<i>But it's just too powerful!</i>

05:13.150 --> 05:15.110
<i>He's going straight into the goal!</i>

05:15.110 --> 05:16.160
Matsuyama!

05:16.160 --> 05:17.450
Captain!

05:18.250 --> 05:22.750
<i>Everyone in front of the goal came to hold Matsuyama!</i>

05:23.260 --> 05:24.210
Matsuyama!

05:24.210 --> 05:27.080
<i>The Drive Shot has been stopped!</i>

05:30.990 --> 05:31.890
Guys...

05:31.890 --> 05:33.150
Captain...

05:33.150 --> 05:37.890
<i>Furano's eleven have become one, and blocked Tsubasa's Drive Shot!</i>

05:37.890 --> 05:39.060
You did it!

05:39.060 --> 05:42.390
See that? This is what Furano's true teamwork looks like!

05:42.390 --> 05:43.240
Damn it...

05:43.240 --> 05:47.600
Tsubasa put all of his might in that Drive Shot, and yet...

05:47.600 --> 05:48.980
Tsubasa...

05:48.980 --> 05:50.490
Damn that Tsubasa...

05:50.490 --> 05:54.490
He had to use the Drive Shot, despite being what strains his body the most...

05:54.490 --> 05:56.750
Guys! We can't afford to take it slow!

05:56.750 --> 05:57.670
We have no time!

05:57.670 --> 05:58.620
Let's attack right now!

05:58.620 --> 06:01.040
It's our turn to score, now!

06:01.040 --> 06:01.740
Yeah!

06:01.740 --> 06:04.580
<i>Another Avalanche Attack from Furano!</i>

06:04.580 --> 06:07.960
<i>With the time that's left, this might just be the final attack.</i>

06:07.960 --> 06:13.120
<i>Regardless of my going to the US when they lose... I just want to see them win! </i>

06:13.120 --> 06:15.560
<i>Matsuyama and everyone have worked so hard to get here.</i>

06:15.560 --> 06:16.970
<i>I want you to make them win!</i>

06:16.970 --> 06:18.510
Damn it!

06:20.430 --> 06:22.970
<i>Tsubasa, this is the final showdown!</i>

06:22.970 --> 06:24.430
<i>I will definitely pass through!</i>

06:24.430 --> 06:25.980
<i>I... shall not lose!</i>

06:25.980 --> 06:26.690
<i>I... shall not lose! </i>

06:27.690 --> 06:29.960
<i>Very little time is left!</i>

06:29.960 --> 06:33.190
<i>This has become a fierce #10 vs. #10 fight again!</i>

06:37.450 --> 06:39.200
Good luck, Tsubasa!

06:39.200 --> 06:40.950
Break through, Matsuyama!

06:40.950 --> 06:43.200
Matsuyama!

06:43.200 --> 06:51.960
Tsubasa!

06:43.690 --> 06:47.190
<i>The stadium is filled with divided cheers for Matsuyama and for Tsubasa!</i>

06:47.190 --> 06:50.010
<i>Who will emerge victorious in the end?</i>

06:50.010 --> 06:51.960
<i>Neither side yields!</i>

07:01.760 --> 07:03.340
<i>I won't let you take the ball from me!</i>

07:03.340 --> 07:05.100
<i>I'll use my control to get past you!</i>

07:05.100 --> 07:06.600
<i>Like I'd let you pass!</i>

07:06.600 --> 07:08.050
Captain...

07:08.050 --> 07:09.670
Let's believe in our captain.

07:09.670 --> 07:11.610
We should go up to the front of the goal!

07:11.610 --> 07:13.690
Tsubasa's almost at his limit.

07:13.690 --> 07:15.350
We should help him!

07:15.350 --> 07:16.110
Yeah!

07:16.110 --> 07:19.110
<i>Nankatsu's going to support Tsubasa!</i>

07:19.110 --> 07:23.410
<i>If Furano takes the ball now, they'll have no one but the goalkeeper left behind.</i>

07:25.330 --> 07:27.660
If I said I'd pass you, it means that I'll pass you!

07:28.850 --> 07:31.330
<i>The two clash fiercely!</i>

07:32.420 --> 07:33.670
Tsubasa!

07:33.670 --> 07:36.280
<i>But it isn't a foul!</i>

07:36.280 --> 07:41.180
<i>Football is a physical sport! You can't always avoid hits like that one.</i>

07:41.180 --> 07:42.130
Damn it!

07:42.130 --> 07:44.180
This time we'll have to stop you!

07:44.610 --> 07:45.680
Here I go!

07:47.680 --> 07:48.540
What?

07:48.540 --> 07:49.270
Crap!

07:49.270 --> 07:51.500
<i>He got past Kisugi and Taki!</i>

07:51.500 --> 07:55.770
<i>And that's why they say he's got the best control; the Wild Eagle of Hokkaido, Hikaru Matsuyama!</i>

07:55.770 --> 07:57.320
We will defend!

07:58.240 --> 08:00.860
<i>Matsuyama gets in position to shoot.</i>

08:00.860 --> 08:02.740
<i>Will it be his Northern Country Shot?</i>

08:02.740 --> 08:07.870
We will block your shot this time to pay you back for stopping Tsubasa's Drive Shot.

08:07.870 --> 08:08.870
What?!

08:08.870 --> 08:11.420
<i>Matsuyama switches it to a pass.</i>

08:11.420 --> 08:13.730
<i>He's left the finishing blow to his friends!</i>

08:13.730 --> 08:14.600
Let's go!

08:14.600 --> 08:16.960
We'll definitely get captain's pass into that goal!

08:16.960 --> 08:18.000
Damn it!

08:18.000 --> 08:22.420
<i>We are tied with the threads of friendship and trust.</i>

08:22.420 --> 08:23.720
<i>I'm leaving it to you, guys!</i>

08:27.850 --> 08:30.110
<i>It's in!</i>

08:30.110 --> 08:31.160
<i>It's a tie!</i>

08:31.160 --> 08:33.400
<i>Furano's persistence has let us witness their true potential!</i>

08:34.900 --> 08:36.900
We did it, guys!

08:36.900 --> 08:38.150
Captain!

08:38.150 --> 08:38.810
We did it!

08:38.810 --> 08:39.860
We caught up!

08:39.860 --> 08:40.900
It's a tie!

08:40.900 --> 08:43.150
We did it Yoshiko! The game is tied!

08:43.150 --> 08:45.030
I'm so glad, guys!

08:45.710 --> 08:49.600
<i>So you couldn't hold out till the end, Tsubasa...</i>

08:49.600 --> 08:54.880
<i>If you didn't go for a Drive Shot there, you might have preserved your one-goal lead.</i>

08:54.880 --> 08:59.670
<i>But you chose to score... You chose to attack instead of defending what you've got.</i>

08:59.670 --> 09:02.060
Damn it! They caught up with us!

09:02.060 --> 09:03.950
We didn't even have a minute left!

09:03.950 --> 09:05.300
Damn it!

09:07.840 --> 09:09.310
Tsubasa...

09:09.310 --> 09:12.220
The game's not over yet, guys.

09:13.560 --> 09:16.310
Tsubasa!

09:16.750 --> 09:19.320
<i>There's less than a minute left.</i>

09:19.320 --> 09:21.320
<i>First and second halves; 60 minutes.</i>

09:21.320 --> 09:24.550
<i>Tsubasa, I couldn't win against you.</i>

09:24.550 --> 09:26.820
<i>But I didn't lose, either.</i>

09:26.820 --> 09:28.820
<i>Stand up, Tsubasa.</i>

09:28.820 --> 09:30.820
<i>I'll take you on in the penalty shoot-outs.</i>

09:34.830 --> 09:37.080
<i>Tsubasa stood up!</i>

09:37.080 --> 09:40.510
<i>He got back on his feet while holding his left shoulder.</i>

09:40.510 --> 09:42.210
Are you okay, Tsubasa?

09:42.210 --> 09:43.740
Kisugi, Taki.

09:43.740 --> 09:46.340
When the game resumes, send me a pass right away.

09:46.340 --> 09:48.180
What are you talking about, Tsubasa?

09:48.180 --> 09:49.410
In your current condition...

09:49.410 --> 09:50.300
He's right.

09:50.300 --> 09:51.980
It's impossible, even for you...

09:51.980 --> 09:53.730
Just send a pass to Tsubasa.

09:55.940 --> 09:59.390
Tsubasa is Nankatsu's captain. Our captain.

09:59.390 --> 10:01.860
We should obey our captain's orders until the end.

10:01.860 --> 10:03.900
Ishizaki...

10:08.940 --> 10:11.160
I'm counting on you, Captain Tsubasa.

10:11.720 --> 10:13.290
Ishizaki...

10:15.790 --> 10:18.440
All right, we should follow our captain too.

10:18.440 --> 10:19.410
Yeah.

10:21.790 --> 10:26.280
<i>Tsubasa will be going to Brazil
when he graduates from middle school.</i>

10:26.280 --> 10:31.810
<i>However, even if we were to lose today's match, I have no regrets in my middle school football life.</i>

10:32.460 --> 10:37.560
<i>Because I've been playing football with you all this time, Tsubasa.</i>

10:42.440 --> 10:47.700
Sign: CERTAIN VICTORY

10:43.400 --> 10:44.940
<i>Thank you, everyone.</i>

10:44.940 --> 10:47.700
<i>I'll bet everything on this last chance.</i>

10:47.700 --> 10:52.200
<i>Normally, he would be standing in front and facing us now, even with this little time left.</i>

10:52.860 --> 10:55.700
<i>Has your flame died down already, Tsubasa?</i>

10:56.370 --> 10:57.620
<i>The game resumes.</i>

10:58.160 --> 10:59.580
<i>The ball is sent to Tsubasa.</i>

10:59.580 --> 11:00.940
Let's go!

11:01.710 --> 11:04.090
Tsubasa, you were still hanging on to this match...?

11:04.090 --> 11:07.470
<i>Tsubasa is getting into position to shoot.</i>

11:08.630 --> 11:12.590
<i>My shoulder, my leg; break, if you will!</i>

11:12.590 --> 11:14.180
<i>But I... I will shoot!</i>

11:16.180 --> 11:18.100
My Drive Shot will...

11:18.850 --> 11:22.610
spread its wings to the vast sky!

11:24.190 --> 11:27.510
<i>Tsubasa fires off a super long shot.</i>

11:27.510 --> 11:30.640
<i>Matsuyama jumped, but couldn't block it!</i>

11:31.700 --> 11:34.100
<i>The phoenix is in flight!</i>

11:38.040 --> 11:42.710
<i>The ball follows a sharp line and and continues its path towards Furano's goal.</i>

11:44.970 --> 11:47.210
<i>Nankatsu can't score!</i>

11:47.210 --> 11:48.720
Damn it!

11:48.720 --> 11:52.430
<i>The Drive Shot fell short of becoming a goal!</i>

11:55.680 --> 11:57.180
That is...

11:59.600 --> 12:00.140
What?!

12:00.980 --> 12:06.230
<i>The ball hit the ground, rebounded and pierced into the goal!</i>

12:06.700 --> 12:09.240
<i>The spin on the ball is insane!</i>

12:14.690 --> 12:16.040
It's in.

12:26.520 --> 12:29.670
<i>It's 3-2! What a shocking finale!</i>

12:29.670 --> 12:32.630
<i>Tsubasa's Drive Shot soared like a phoenix!</i>

12:32.630 --> 12:36.290
<i>It refused to die until the last, very last minute!</i>

12:36.290 --> 12:38.940
<i>Nankatsu win their seat in the final match tomorrow!</i>

12:38.940 --> 12:40.640
Tsubasa is so cool!

12:40.640 --> 12:41.890
We did it!

12:41.890 --> 12:42.730
We won!

12:42.730 --> 12:44.520
We won, Tsubasa!

12:44.520 --> 12:47.040
<i>The man who brings forth miracles!</i>

12:47.040 --> 12:49.540
<i>Within the five seconds after the kick-off whistle,</i>

12:49.540 --> 12:52.340
<i>Tsubasa's Drive Shot pulled them away from Furano,</i>

12:52.340 --> 12:56.520
<i>and they've managed to take their place in the finals for the third time in a row!</i>

12:56.520 --> 12:58.600
We won!

12:59.330 --> 13:00.240
Oh!

13:00.240 --> 13:01.000
Tsubasa!

13:03.420 --> 13:05.340
What's with you, Tsubasa?

13:05.340 --> 13:07.810
We can't have a victor fall to the ground here.

13:07.810 --> 13:09.130
Matsuyama...

13:09.130 --> 13:10.860
Really though, Tsubasa...

13:10.860 --> 13:15.080
You really are a man who just will not give up on a battle until the very end.

13:15.080 --> 13:17.890
That last Drive Shot was proof of that.

13:17.890 --> 13:22.180
It didn't die even after hitting the goal post, and jumped into the goal.

13:22.180 --> 13:24.650
It's just like you.

13:26.520 --> 13:28.490
Now, get a hang of yourself.

13:28.490 --> 13:32.070
You still have the final game tomorrow.

13:32.070 --> 13:34.320
Thanks, Matsuyama.

13:36.880 --> 13:38.060
We lost...

13:38.060 --> 13:40.530
We lost at the very end!

13:40.530 --> 13:41.830
Damn it!

13:41.830 --> 13:43.100
<i>Guys...</i>

13:43.990 --> 13:45.260
Get on your feet, guys.

13:45.260 --> 13:48.960
We're gonna thank the people in the stands who were with us this entire time, one last time.

13:49.780 --> 13:50.920
Captain.

13:50.920 --> 13:54.920
<i>Furano's players, who fought hard but lost in the end, are going to salute the fans.</i>

13:55.680 --> 14:00.180
<i>You have really fought well until today, refreshing warriors from the snowy lands.</i>

14:00.180 --> 14:01.670
Guys...

14:01.670 --> 14:03.020
Matsuyama...

14:03.020 --> 14:05.120
Guys, get in line.

14:06.190 --> 14:08.770
Thanks a lot for your support!

14:08.770 --> 14:10.530
You did well, Furano!

14:10.530 --> 14:14.510
Even if you are defeated, your teamwork is still the best in Japan.

14:16.870 --> 14:22.290
<i>Hikaru Matsuyama, despite your loss, you are a man amongst men!</i>

14:23.230 --> 14:26.510
<i>Our football is over now.</i>

14:28.540 --> 14:31.410
Yoshiko, don't cry anymore.

14:31.410 --> 14:32.690
Yoshiko.

14:32.690 --> 14:33.960
Mom.

14:33.960 --> 14:36.220
It was unfortunate, no?

14:36.220 --> 14:38.220
Yes.

14:38.940 --> 14:39.930
Oh!

14:42.650 --> 14:44.600
It's Matsuyama's headband.

14:45.540 --> 14:47.100
Hey, Matsuyama!

14:47.100 --> 14:49.080
You forgot something.

14:49.080 --> 14:50.310
Oh, thanks.

14:50.910 --> 14:52.330
Appreciate it.

14:52.330 --> 14:54.980
Do your best and help Tsubasa tomorrow, too.

14:54.980 --> 14:56.170
Sure.

14:57.490 --> 15:02.110
It seems the final will be held between Nankatsu and Toho, as we'd projected.

15:02.110 --> 15:03.200
Yeah.

15:04.420 --> 15:06.450
Tsubasa's Drive Shot...

15:06.450 --> 15:11.840
I really want to see the battle between it and Genzo on our tour of Europe as soon as possible.

15:11.840 --> 15:15.150
Either way, we need to get you to my hospital.

15:15.150 --> 15:17.150
I would like you to prepare the car.

15:17.150 --> 15:18.220
Yeah, sure.

15:18.220 --> 15:19.600
Good grief.

15:19.600 --> 15:21.720
You went too far again, despite me warning you.

15:21.720 --> 15:26.190
I couldn't have won if I didn't go that far.

15:26.190 --> 15:27.980
I wanted to win.

15:27.980 --> 15:29.850
Tsubasa.

15:29.850 --> 15:32.490
It's thanks to you, doctor.

15:32.490 --> 15:36.860
It's thanks to your treatment and the words you wrote here.

15:36.860 --> 15:39.160
Did you write those words, doctor?

15:39.160 --> 15:40.310
Yeah.

15:40.310 --> 15:44.050
I told him that my handwriting is really bad, but he wanted me to do it, anyway.

15:45.240 --> 15:46.490
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL
HOKKAIDO

15:47.910 --> 15:50.910
<i>The headband our manager put effort into and crafted...</i>

15:51.610 --> 15:54.920
<i>Sorry, I couldn't win.</i>

16:00.610 --> 16:02.180
<i>This is...</i>

16:03.040 --> 16:05.000
<i>She sewed this writing in here, and it's so small...</i>

16:05.000 --> 16:08.930
<i>And she even made sure it wouldn't stand out, embroidering it with a white thread...</i>

16:09.780 --> 16:11.270
Let me through!

16:11.730 --> 16:12.770
Fujisawa!

16:13.510 --> 16:20.360
<i>Yoshiko Fujisawa will be moving to the US in the second term, due to her father's work.</i>

16:24.290 --> 16:25.870
Matsuyama!

16:25.870 --> 16:27.080
Machida!

16:27.080 --> 16:28.150
Where did Fujisawa go?

16:28.150 --> 16:30.460
She went with her mom; she's getting a taxi.

16:30.460 --> 16:31.220
Wha–

16:31.220 --> 16:34.460
Yoshiko is leaving to the US today.

16:34.460 --> 16:35.730
So, where is their car?!

16:35.730 --> 16:38.920
Matsuyama, Yoshiko had feelings...

16:38.920 --> 16:41.760
<i>What's the matter? Do you need me?</i>

16:41.760 --> 16:44.010
<i>D-do your best and win today too!</i>

16:44.010 --> 16:46.330
<i>Being a manager must be tough.</i>

16:47.700 --> 16:49.660
<i>Please make a copy of this.</i>

16:49.660 --> 16:50.970
<i>Sure.</i>

16:50.970 --> 16:52.580
<i>Come on, you first-grader kid!</i>

16:52.580 --> 16:55.360
<i>Don't make our manager polish all the balls herself.</i>

16:56.250 --> 16:57.750
<i>Here, a towel.</i>

16:57.750 --> 16:59.280
<i>Furano, fight!</i>

16:59.740 --> 17:01.280
<i>Fujisawa...</i>

17:06.240 --> 17:07.660
Is that the car?

17:07.660 --> 17:10.660
Yoshiko, wipe your tears already.

17:14.590 --> 17:15.790
Fujisawa!

17:28.150 --> 17:29.380
Fujisawa...

17:32.430 --> 17:33.750
Is that so?

17:33.750 --> 17:35.790
Fujisawa has left already.

17:35.790 --> 17:36.660
Yes.

17:36.660 --> 17:38.440
She sends her regards to everyone.

17:38.440 --> 17:42.770
If we had won, she would have stayed in Japan one more day...

17:42.770 --> 17:45.200
So, Captain went to see Fujisawa off?

17:45.200 --> 17:49.530
He went after the taxi, but there's no way he made it in time.

17:49.530 --> 17:50.950
Is that so?

17:50.950 --> 17:54.220
Actually, Yoshiko always had feelings for Matsuyama...

17:54.220 --> 17:55.520
Well, no surprise here.

17:56.000 --> 17:59.340
We actually always assumed that was the case.

17:59.340 --> 18:01.500
You could tell just by watching her.

18:01.500 --> 18:05.510
But our captain is quite thick-headed when it comes to things like this.

18:05.510 --> 18:10.350
So, wait a sec... Why did captain go after Fujisawa right now?

18:10.350 --> 18:11.390
Now that you said it...

18:11.390 --> 18:14.020
Well, it's no use if he doesn't make it.

18:14.020 --> 18:17.480
So Yoshiko will leave without confessing her feelings after all.

18:31.530 --> 18:32.790
Fujisawa!

18:32.790 --> 18:34.370
Matsuyama.

18:41.090 --> 18:43.380
It looks like I've made it.

18:43.380 --> 18:45.050
How?

18:45.050 --> 18:49.760
Well, after your taxi drove away, a guy from the Football Federation gave me a lift.

18:49.760 --> 18:52.850
I asked him to drive as fast as he could, too.

18:52.850 --> 18:56.520
Forget making it in time, it looks like we even caught up with and passed you!

18:56.520 --> 18:58.600
Oh, Matsuyama! You're bleeding!

18:58.600 --> 18:59.770
Huh?

19:02.230 --> 19:03.740
Oh, it's fine, really.

19:03.740 --> 19:05.010
But, your handkerchief...

19:05.010 --> 19:07.530
No! You're bleeding too much...

19:08.540 --> 19:12.910
This will be the last time you treat my wounds like this.

19:12.910 --> 19:17.910
You always play recklessly, so you wind up getting hurt the most, Matsuyama.

19:19.240 --> 19:21.650
You know, I'd rather you said "bravely".

19:21.650 --> 19:24.460
Here, press down on this with your hand for a bit.

19:24.460 --> 19:26.170
Thank you, Manager.

19:28.970 --> 19:30.720
What's wrong?

19:31.390 --> 19:35.720
It's because you just appeared here out of nowhere.

19:35.720 --> 19:36.900
What does that even mean...?

19:36.900 --> 19:38.460
It's your fault.

19:38.460 --> 19:41.320
I yelled at you, "Fujisawa!" while I ran after the taxi,

19:41.320 --> 19:43.860
but you didn't notice and just drove away...

19:43.860 --> 19:46.610
I hurt my knee then, too.

19:46.610 --> 19:47.580
Hey...

19:47.580 --> 19:48.610
Don't cry.

19:48.610 --> 19:49.990
But...

19:49.990 --> 19:51.740
I'm telling you to not cry.

19:51.740 --> 19:56.350
You can't even wipe your tears, your handkerchief is on my knee, you know.

19:56.350 --> 19:57.290
Matsuyama!

20:01.980 --> 20:04.000
Take care of yourself. Make sure you come back.

20:04.000 --> 20:04.790
Sure.

20:05.410 --> 20:07.490
Send me some e-mails when you get there.

20:07.490 --> 20:09.470
I'll be sure to reply.

20:09.470 --> 20:10.220
Okay.

20:10.970 --> 20:17.300
Also, I will keep this headband as a memoir from you.

20:17.300 --> 20:18.440
Thanks.

20:19.060 --> 20:19.890
Sure.

20:28.030 --> 20:29.680
Captain sure is taking his time...

20:29.680 --> 20:30.990
I wonder how far he went.

20:30.990 --> 20:33.500
Don't tell me he chased them to the airport?!

20:33.500 --> 20:34.530
Yeah, right.

20:34.530 --> 20:36.850
He doesn't have that kind of money on him, you know!

20:36.850 --> 20:37.900
Coach, sir.

20:37.900 --> 20:40.290
You have a call from the young sir, Matsuyama.

20:40.290 --> 20:40.740
Huh?

20:40.740 --> 20:42.000
Matsuyama, you say?

20:42.790 --> 20:44.000
I'm really sorry, coach.

20:44.410 --> 20:46.750
I'm on my way back from Narita Airport.

20:46.750 --> 20:47.750
What?

20:47.750 --> 20:52.030
I will get dropped off at the lodging house directly, so please, don't worry.

20:52.030 --> 20:53.630
All right, got it.

20:54.260 --> 20:57.260
Good for you, right, Yoshiko?

20:59.310 --> 21:02.660
<i>Like I expected, the finals will be between Nankatsu and Toho.</i>

21:02.660 --> 21:05.520
<i>In the end, it came down to Tsubasa Ozora versus Kojiro Hyuga.</i>

21:06.180 --> 21:08.540
<i>However, Hyuga's situation bothers me.</i>

21:08.540 --> 21:11.030
<i>Will he play in tomorrow's final?</i>

21:11.690 --> 21:18.200
<i>To be frank, Hyuga's growth after entering middle school was quite low compared to everyone's expectations.</i>

21:18.830 --> 21:23.750
<i>The boy who, with nothing else but his burning fighting spirit in the elementary school tournament,</i>

21:23.750 --> 21:28.210
<i>made Nankatsu's Tsubasa, Misaki and Wakabayashi struggle so much by himself... Kojiro Hyuga.</i>

21:29.150 --> 21:35.640
<i>After he went to Toho Academy, his style of football, reminiscent of a starving beast, just disappeared.</i>

21:35.640 --> 21:39.770
<i>From the bottom of my heart, I wish for the return of the Ferocious Tiger,</i>

21:39.770 --> 21:41.640
<i>for the sake of Japan's football.</i>

21:42.090 --> 21:44.380
<i>After Tsubasa leaves for Brazil,</i>

21:44.380 --> 21:47.900
<i>the only person we can leave Japan's football to</i>

21:47.900 --> 21:50.400
<i>is you, Hyuga.</i>

22:09.460 --> 22:12.970
Oh, coach, a letter arrived this morning.

22:12.970 --> 22:14.300
Sure, thank you.

22:17.010 --> 22:20.010
KOZO KIRA

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.780
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.780
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.200 --> 23:21.250
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.000 --> 23:33.340
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.000 --> 23:33.340
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.340 --> 23:39.390
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.520 --> 23:59.060
COMING UP, EPISODE 46:
THE KICK-OFF OF THE CENTURY
